A||N||12||Will||Northstar & LS1||||1||
Z||000000||Will||06-02-2000||12:44 PM||||Greetings!<BR>I am the bloke referred to here: &lt;http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/004068.html&gt;<P>I have a question or two for the illustrious users of this forum:<P>I am trying to use LS1 electronics to run a Cadillac Northstar that will go into my '86 SE. The problem is that the N* and LS1 use different crank position sensors. I have been told that a chip could be programmed to translate the N* pulse train into an LS1 pulse train, but I would need to know with a high degree of accuracy what each pulse train looks like. Can anyone help? Does anyone know who I could call to get this information?<P>TIA<P>P.S. If any one is interested, I have successfully retrofitted an '88 front suspension into my '86. I'd be glad to share the details.||||reg||1
Z||000001||lennyb4||06-02-2000||01:22 PM||||Welcome to our forum bud. Dont know if you got my e-mail or not. Well i wish i could help you out with your question but thats not really my area. But dont fret, most of the guys get on later in the day and i know for fact of atleast three people who can answer this easily..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
